{"title":"Redux of my advice to DOGE","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/919429625/0/marginalrevolution~Redux-of-my-advice-to-DOGE.html","date":1748718214000,"content":"<p>From <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2024-11-15/how-musk-s-doge-can-actually-do-some-good?sref=htOHjx5Y\" target=\"_blank\">a November Bloomberg column</a>:</p>\r\n<blockquote><p>Many Republicans are very excited about DOGE. But its governance structure is undefined and untested. It does not have a natural home or an enduring constituency. It cannot engage in much favor-trading. Its ability to keep Trump’s attention and loyalty may prove limited. And it’s not clear that deregulation is a priority for many voters.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>Worth a ponder, at the time I advised DOGE to prioritize on a few key areas for maximum impact.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/05/redux-of-my-advice-to-doge.html\">Redux of my advice to DOGE</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/919429625/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/919429625/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/919429625/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/919429625/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/919429625/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/email20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com